workplan/ratification-execution-register-2026-07-13.md:47:Everything else the reviewer attacked (GAP-297's absence pre-C1 / presence post-C1 pulled directly from the pre-C1 DB blob via `git show`; `convergence_assessment`↔`evidence_cell_state` join orphan check beyond the FK check; `v_best_practice` returning 5 rows none RSO; a read of the actual rendered HTML across all 6 audience registers for the CRPD/ethics lens, incl. the Co-1 solo-authorship caveat and the regulatory-stratum "convergence is not evidence" framing; scope check via `git show --stat` confirming only the 3 intended files changed) survived independent re-verification without a finding.
workplan/ratification-execution-register-2026-07-13.md:76:2. **MEDIUM-HIGH — caveat non-survival: the schema's flagship anti-laundering flag and its plain-language explanation were never rendered on any live page.** Neither `population_page.py` nor `spec_page.py` queried or rendered `regulatory_stratum_only`, `confidence_synthesis_basis`, `has_unverified_sources`, or `all_sources_disqualified`; `population_page.py`'s determinations table also omitted `falsification_condition` (present on spec pages, absent on population pages) and left `item_code` as unlinked plain text unlike every other cross-reference on the page. Concretely: E-06×MOB (`regulatory_stratum_only=1`, "the decisive G1 cell" per this register's own C1 entry) rendered identically to a normal `code_floor_only=no` row before this fix — the exact "convergence-laundering" outcome `governance/evidence-architecture.md` and `DR-2026-07-12-evidence-architecture-unification.md` name this column as existing to prevent, now live on the public site. This predates C2 (the generator code is unchanged since before migration 027 added the column) but was invisible until C2 made real determinations live — a "not yet computed" banner covered for it until now. **Fixed:** both generators now select and render `regulatory_stratum_only` (new column, same yes/no style as `code_floor_only`), `confidence_synthesis_basis` (the qualitative caveat sentence, rendered verbatim), and a `source_caveats()` helper surfacing `has_unverified_sources`/`all_sources_disqualified` as `UNVERIFIED-1`/`ALL-DISQUALIFIED` badges; `population_page.py` gained `falsification_condition` and a hyperlinked `item_code`. VERIFIED-BY: regenerated `mob.html` and `e-12.html` to scratch paths after the fix — E-06's row now reads `regulatory_stratum_only=yes` with its full "NOT an evidence-anchored best practice: no anchoring dimension exists" sentence rendered; E-12's row now reads `UNVERIFIED-1` in the source-caveats column.
workplan/ratification-execution-register-2026-07-13.md:117:2. **`workplan/best-practices-assessment-system.md` §4's stale SQL sketch — FIXED.** Contradicted the ratified, DB-live `evidence_cell_state` schema (migration 026: keyed on `item_code`/`population_code`, not `slug`/`population`/`jurisdiction`). Zero judgment call: `decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-cell-state-schema-reconciliation.md`'s own "Consequences if ratified" section already states this file is superseded — nobody had synced that fact into the file itself. Added a superseded banner quoting the DR verbatim; sketch left in place for its still-relevant §8 phasing-plan context.
workplan/ratification-execution-register-2026-07-13.md:121:6. **NEW — STI acoustic-threshold three-way conflict, not previously tracked.** `references/bpc/sensory-environment/acoustics-speech-intelligibility-disability.md` states a flat "STI ≥0.5"; `references/bpc/sensory-environment/room-acoustic-performance.md` has already internally adjudicated to "STI ≥0.60 general / ≥0.75 DEAF-CI" (its own audit trail: RAP-C3 "✅ CONFIRMED — Tier 1 evidence, not contradicted"); `references/bpc/DEAF.md`'s third framing ("0.50 minimum / 0.60 best practice") is moot — that file is marked `FROZEN — historical archive... any skill reading this file is in error`, so it should never have been in the comparison set to begin with, per its own header. VERIFIED-BY: direct read of all four files' current content and header banners, this session. **The twist that blocks a point-fix:** all three live candidates carry the identical `PRE-REHABILITATION — RETRACTED PENDING REVERIFICATION` banner (DR-2026-05-23 cohort) — including room-acoustic-performance.md's own "confirmed" 0.75 figure. Picking a number now, even the seemingly-adjudicated one, would be exactly the premature-synthesis the retraction banner exists to prevent. **Recommended resolution:** flag this as a named item for the Phase E.2g reverification pass (the same mechanism GAP-269 uses for the corridor-width conflict), not a same-session number pick. Tracked as Q24.
